  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "3D HTS coil manufacturing is feasible — REBCO tape can be wound onto complex non-planar modular coil forms at 12.5 m major radius scale without exceeding bending strain limits",
      "Quasi-isodynamic (4-field-period, maximum-J) optimization delivers Q > 40 with 800 MW fusion power at R = 12.5 m, A = 10, 9 T on-axis, validated by 70,000+ configuration simulations on DOE Frontier",
      "HCPB blanket with Li4SiO4/Li2TiO3 pebbles and Be multiplier achieves TBR = 1.30 (OpenMC-confirmed) when adapted from EU-DEMO tokamak geometry to non-axisymmetric stellarator first wall",
      "Island divertor (classical W7-X heritage or novel LIBD) can exhaust helium ash adequately over 2-year continuous operating cycles at burning plasma heat fluxes",
      "2-year operating cycles with 30-day planned maintenance outages deliver ~96% theoretical capacity factor, enabling steady-state advantage to offset large-machine capital cost",
      "CFS partnership successfully transfers flat-coil REBCO manufacturing experience to 3D stellarator geometry, validated through the Infinity One subscale program by 2029",
      "m=5, n=4 island chain selection avoids ι=1 resonances sufficiently that error field correction coils are not required at manufacturing-scale field errors"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No current drive system (capital and recirculating power) — stellarator is inherently steady-state, no plasma current required",
      "No central solenoid — removes a major tokamak capital item",
      "No disruption management system and no disruption-repair O&M — stellarators do not disrupt in optimized operation",
      "No thermal energy storage / buffering in BOP — genuine steady-state operation delivers constant thermal power, unlike pulsed concepts",
      "No niobium-based LTS supply dependency — REBCO HTS throughout removes Nb3Sn/NbTi from the supply chain"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "3D non-planar HTS modular coil manufacturing — no cost precedent at any scale for winding REBCO tape onto complex curved forms; dominant capital sensitivity (elasticity +0.99)",
      "Island divertor system (classical or LIBD) — complex 3D target geometry with no published unit cost and no commercial supply chain; LIBD adds active cooling in constrained island-interior access geometry",
      "Stellarator-geometry HCPB blanket modules — non-axisymmetric first wall requires custom module design and interfaces differing from EU-DEMO tokamak heritage",
      "Remote maintenance system for non-axisymmetric geometry — no standard cask or central solenoid removal pathway; bespoke tooling for Infinity Two-specific blanket, divertor, and coil access",
      "Potential error field correction coil system — unbudgeted auxiliary coils, power supplies, and cryogenics if manufacturing-scale field errors require correction despite m=5, n=4 design intent"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "3D HTS coil manufacturing has no cost precedent; framework default C220103 = $2.3B is acknowledged lower bound, 3×–5× premium plausible driving LCOE from $306 to $840/MWh at 350 MWe",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO tape bending strain limit (~25-30 mm minimum radius) may be challenged by QI-optimized 3D coil cross-section curvature — feasibility not demonstrated at any scale",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Classical island divertor particle exhaust efficiency (0.44%–2.9%) falls at or below required range (0.5%–5%) — marginal helium ash removal over 2-year cycles under conservative transport assumptions",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "LIBD alternative divertor is TRL 2–3 with no experimental validation; dome geometry inside island interior has unresolved perpendicular-transport risk and cooling-access challenges",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Li-6 enrichment supply is effectively zero in the West — COLEX banned under Minamata Convention, ICOMAX decades from scale; creates path-critical HCPB deployment risk on Infinity Two timeline",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Capital cost, overnight construction cost, and thermal efficiency are all unpublished; no ARIES-CS-equivalent plant study exists for Infinity Two — blocks independent LCOE validation",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium stockpile depletion projected from ~2035 by Pearson coincides with Type One Energy's mid-2030s deployment target — startup inventory cost ($35,000/g) and availability may worsen materially",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Availability uncertainty spans 80%–96% with no observational constraint; elasticity −0.93 makes this a co-dominant LCOE driver alongside coil cost, but often omitted from sensitivity reporting",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Infinity One→Infinity Two timeline gap — successful 2029 subscale verification plus construction lead time makes mid-2030s first plasma aggressive; any design iteration from Infinity One results pushes schedule out",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Error field correction coils may be required at manufacturing scale despite m=5, n=4 island chain design intent (W7-X precedent required such coils); unbudgeted CAS22 capital item",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Island divertor target lifetime at burning plasma conditions is unknown — life-limiting availability component with no data at Infinity Two heat flux levels",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Beryllium pebble supply chain at fusion plant scale is uncharacterized — Materion is sole US producer, global supply ~300 t/year, toxic handling requires specialized infrastructure",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "HCPB module replacement interval driven by ~5 dpa Li4SiO4 damage limit implies replacement every few years — O&M cost category not quantified and stellarator-geometry handling is unvalidated",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium extraction from HCPB pebbles at kg/day throughput over 2-year continuous cycles has no experimental basis — breeding shortfall cannot be corrected until scheduled outage",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Regulatory treatment uncertain — Stewart & Shirvan 2.2× building cost factor under fission-style regulation applies to all D-T MFE plants",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
